# How would you deploy multiple LoRA adapters in production?

This is a very important production LLM question.

Imagine you have one base model:

```text
Llama 3.x Base Model
```

but different fine-tuned behaviors:

```text
                    ┌── Finance LoRA
                    │
Base Model ─────────┼── Legal LoRA
                    │
                    ├── Customer A LoRA
                    │
                    ├── Customer B LoRA
                    │
                    └── Medical LoRA
```

You **do not want to load a separate full 8B model for every customer or domain**.

Instead:

> **Load the base model once and dynamically select the appropriate LoRA adapter for each request.**

Modern vLLM supports serving multiple LoRA adapters and selecting an adapter per request; its official docs also expose controls such as `max_loras`, `max_lora_rank`, and CPU caching. ([vLLM][1])

