# 5. Use vLLM to serve multiple adapters

A practical production approach is vLLM.

For example:

```bash
vllm serve meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct \
    --enable-lora \
    --max-loras 8 \
    --max-lora-rank 64 \
    --max-cpu-loras 32 \
    --lora-modules \
        finance=/models/adapters/finance \
        legal=/models/adapters/legal \
        support=/models/adapters/support
```

The vLLM server can expose preloaded adapters as selectable models through its OpenAI-compatible API. Its docs recommend setting `max_lora_rank` to the maximum rank actually required rather than unnecessarily overallocating memory. ([vLLM][1])

